                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To tease (someone) by offering something desirable but keeping it out of reach."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "87933647-01c9-4582-a296-3389bcefc39a",
                                                "sense_id": "ab2b2345-d380-30df-9f74-91e0c62ad2bc",
                                                "text": "The poore people in Corinth did ſee, and ſmell, vvhat the rich men taſted, Tantalizing all the vvhile, and having their penury doubled by the Antiperiſtaſis of others plenty; yea, ryot and exceſſe, for ſome of them vvere drunken."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "84e87b61-39f6-3cb7-ab04-21b07f8f6fb9",
                                        "entry_id": "63ae56d7-994d-371c-b99c-029ca7991837",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To bait (someone) by showing something desirable but leaving them unsatisfied."
                                        ],
